From: substrate
Subject: kdrive/evdev: fix driverPrivate race between RegisterFd + assignment

The kernel TRAP / backtrace pinned the first-client-connect SIGSEGV
to evdev.c:178: `ke->rel[events[i].code] += events[i].value;` with
CR2=0x00000000 — `ke = pi->driverPrivate` came in NULL.

Looking at EvdevPtrEnable, the install order is wrong:

    if (!KdRegisterFd(fd, EvdevPtrRead, pi))   /* fd live NOW */
        ...;
    pi->driverPrivate = ke;                    /* set LATER */

The moment KdRegisterFd returns, the fd is in the X server's select
set.  If a mouse event has been queued (substrate's poll() repolls
every ~10 ms during boot), KdWakeupHandler can dispatch
EvdevPtrRead with closure=pi BEFORE the `pi->driverPrivate = ke`
store completes.  EvdevPtrRead immediately dereferences
pi->driverPrivate → 0x0 SIGSEGV.

Confirmed backtrace from substrate's kernel TRAP log:
    EvdevPtrRead at evdev.c:178
    KdWakeupHandler at kinput.c:2010
    WakeupHandler at dixutils.c:425
    WaitForSomething at WaitFor.c:230
    Dispatch / dix_main / main / _start

Two fixes:

1. Install pi->driverPrivate BEFORE KdRegisterFd in EvdevPtrEnable.

2. NULL-guard EvdevPtrRead defensively — even with the ordering fix,
   EvdevPtrDisable clears driverPrivate, and a wakeup already in
   flight at that point can still arrive at EvdevPtrRead with a
   stale closure.  Drain the read() and return safely.

--- a/hw/kdrive/linux/evdev.c
+++ b/hw/kdrive/linux/evdev.c
@@ -150,11 +150,21 @@ EvdevPtrRead(int evdevPort, void *closure)
 {
     KdPointerInfo *pi = closure;
-    Kevdev *ke = pi->driverPrivate;
+    Kevdev *ke;
     int i;
     struct input_event events[NUM_EVENTS];
     int n;

+    /* Defensive — see EvdevPtrEnable's note about install ordering.
+     * Even with the ordering fix, EvdevPtrDisable may have cleared
+     * driverPrivate while a pending wakeup was still in flight. */
+    if (!pi || !pi->driverPrivate) {
+        char drain[64];
+        (void)read(evdevPort, drain, sizeof(drain));
+        return;
+    }
+    ke = pi->driverPrivate;
+
     n = read(evdevPort, &events, NUM_EVENTS * sizeof(struct input_event));

@@ -298,11 +308,18 @@ EvdevPtrEnable(KdPointerInfo * pi)
-    if (!KdRegisterFd(fd, EvdevPtrRead, pi)) {
-        free(ke);
-        close(fd);
-        return BadAlloc;
-    }
-    pi->driverPrivate = ke;
-    ke->fd = fd;
+    /* IMPORTANT: install driverPrivate BEFORE KdRegisterFd.  The fd
+     * is in the select set the moment KdRegisterFd returns, so an
+     * input event arriving in the window between RegisterFd and
+     * pi->driverPrivate = ke (a handful of instructions, but real
+     * on a busy boot) lands in EvdevPtrRead with driverPrivate==NULL
+     * and crashes the server at `ke->rel[...]`. */
+    ke->fd = fd;
+    pi->driverPrivate = ke;
+    if (!KdRegisterFd(fd, EvdevPtrRead, pi)) {
+        pi->driverPrivate = NULL;
+        free(ke);
+        close(fd);
+        return BadAlloc;
+    }

     return Success;
 }
